# Li - Ugur interatomic potential, hard truncation, with the angular factor
#
# pair_style ugur/ang
# pair_coeff * * Li.ugur.ang Li
#
# Truncation: hard - phi2 does not vanish at rcut2, it stops at -3.65 meV (0.143 of k_B T at 296 K).  USE for static properties and for lattice dynamics: measured against the measured dispersion the hard sets average 9.7 % over the 33 elements that have one, against 12.6 % for the switched sets, and are closer in 25 of them.  DO NOT use for molecular dynamics: copper, whose step is 8.4 meV, drifts 350 meV/atom/ns in NVE and climbs from 296 K to over 1100 K in 200 ps
# MD: DO NOT USE.  At 600 K this structure disintegrates - 432 atoms become 10 and LAMMPS stops.
#
# Lattice stability: screened on the 8^3 and 9^3 meshes AND along the
# symmetry path; no imaginary modes.
#
# Nudge test: passed - displaced by 1e-5 A and relaxed, the lattice returns.
#
# Fitted to: cohesive energy, lattice constant, bulk modulus and the elastic
# constants of Li at its experimental lattice constant.  Nothing else.
#
# Format is LAMMPS's Tersoff convention - one line per ordered triple
# (centre, leg, leg) - so that this file and a multi-element one are read the
# same way.  For a single element that is one line.
#
# el1 el2 el3  m D alpha r0 gamma C alpha3 rcut2 rcut3 taper lam2 lam4
Li Li Li 1.2000025846486944 0.1090562956940829 0.98141002338038386 4.181198896758497 1.4417006236934222e-06 10.172237144376272 5.1040726767646003 9.0766000000000009 4.5349420269172134 -1 1.8999976997612491 1.199972294063687
